diff --git a/CHANGES/v2.11.md b/CHANGES/v2.11.md
index 8be65de0e5..8f476dcdb5 100644
--- a/CHANGES/v2.11.md
+++ b/CHANGES/v2.11.md
@@ -449,6 +449,13 @@ The entries below give the details; the main cases are:
 
 #### Core, performance and input
 
+  - With MPI, the matrices of [CONTACT_MATRIX](CONTACT_MATRIX.md) and of the functions of matrices (e.g. the spherical harmonics of [Q6](Q6.md)) that are only used
+    by functions of matrices and by [MATRIX_VECTOR_PRODUCT](MATRIX_VECTOR_PRODUCT.md) (as in [COORDINATIONNUMBER](COORDINATIONNUMBER.md), [Q6](Q6.md), [LOCAL_AVERAGE](LOCAL_AVERAGE.md))
+    are computed row by row, each row on one process, and are not summed over the processes, nor are the forces on them;
+    each process also clears and copies only its rows of these matrices.
+    The sums were larger than the calculation itself, so that these actions were slower with more MPI processes:
+    on a 32-core node, [Q6](Q6.md) of 20000 atoms took 4.6 s per step with 32 processes and 1.8 s with one, and now takes 1.9 s with 32 and 1.25 s with 4.
+
   - The values and the forces of the functions of vectors and matrices (e.g. the spherical harmonics of [Q6](Q6.md), [CUSTOM](CUSTOM.md) on matrices) are copied
     between the actions and the task manager in memory order: with many components (26 for [Q6](Q6.md)) each element was a separate cache line.
     [Q6](Q6.md) on 1000 atoms is 17% faster. The results are identical.
